<node>
    <node name="description" channel="inline" format="text/plain" model="Starts sensing data input within a thread on the sender/client with the given identification.

It fills the internal input buffer with those data that were received as input.

Calling this operation is not necessary for channel &#x0022;display&#x0022; on a linux operating system with x window system, since &#x0022;activate/enable&#x0022; catches the events of all client windows.
On a windows operating system, however, one separate event thread is run per window, so that calling &#x0022;feel/sense&#x0022; is necessary."/>
    <node name="examples" channel="file" format="text/plain" model="api-generator/spec/logic/feel/sense/examples.txt"/>
    <node name="properties" channel="file" format="element/part" model="api-generator/spec/logic/feel/sense/properties.cybol"/>
</node>
